	abstract = {The Education for Sustainable Development Research Center (ESDRC), Rikkyo University, was established in 2007 as the first university center for Education for Sustainable Development (ESD) in Japan, funded by the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology (MEXT). As educational programs and research to address global challenges tended to be independently conducted in various fields, such as environmental education, development education, and peace education, the ESDRC decided to emphasize a comprehensive approach by bringing together each field under the banner of ‘ESD’ and, thus, aimed at becoming a network hub for ESD research in the Asia-Pacific region. In such a way, the ESDRC’s aim was to pave the way for young academics to successfully establish their scholarly research in leading fields in sustainability and to grasp the environment as a socioculturally contextualized discourse. © Wageningen Academic Publishers The Netherlands, 2014.},
